<title>VIETNAM: VIETNAM TO AUCTION 150 BLN DONG T-NOTES WEDNESDAY.</title>
<headline>VIETNAM TO AUCTION 150 BLN DONG T-NOTES WEDNESDAY.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam will auction 150 billion dong ($12.83 million) worth of one-year Treasury notes on Wednesday, an official at the State Bank of Vietnam said.</p>
<p>At the last sale of government paper, on August 6, the central bank sold 60 billion dong worth of one-year Treasury notes to domestic institutions at an annual interest rate of 11.2 percent.</p>
<p>The government has held 20 Treasury paper auctions so far this year, through which a total of 1.32 trillion dong worth of Treasury stock has been issued.</p>
<p>($1 = 11,689 dong)</p>
</text>
